Day 0, Day 7, Day 14, Day 21, Day 28, Day 35, Day 42, Day 49, Day 56, Day 63, Day 70, Day 77, Day 84 and Day 0 + 6 months

Self-assesment of pain by VAS

The pain of the treatment will be assessed by the Visual Analogue Scale (VAS) at time T0 on the treated area.

The pain assessed is that felt during the application of the devices. It will be collected from the patient within 5 minutes of application.

The VAS is made up of a 10-centimeter line anchored by two ends of the pain. 10 is the first end being the "maximum pain imaginable" and 0 is the other end being "no pain".

