The change of NIHSS score from baseline at 14(discharge) , 30,60,90 days after administration;

The change of NIHSS score from baseline at 14(discharge) , 30,60,90 days after administration; The NIHSS is a tool used by healthcare providers to objectively quantify the impairment caused by a stroke. The NIHSS is composed of 11 items, each of which scores a specific ability between a 0 and 4. For each item, a score of 0 typically indicates normal function in that specific ability, while a higher score is indicative of some level of impairment. The individual scores from each item are summed in order to calculate a patient's total NIHSS score. The maximum possible score is 42, with the minimum score being a 0.

14(discharge) , 30,60,90 days

