The change in MMSE score compared with baseline at 90 days after administration; Mini-mental state examination (MMSE) can comprehensively, accurately and rapidly reflect the intelligence status and the degree of cognitive impairment of the subjects. The scale includes the following 7 aspects: time orientation, place orientation, immediate memory, attention and numeracy, delayed memory, language, visuospatial. The total score of the scale ranged from 0 to 30. The test scores are closely related to the educational level.

